    {
      "id": "mechanism",
      "text": "A fan blows air under the hull, and a rubber skirt traps it. That air pushes barely harder than the air outside. But it pushes on the whole underside, and over that much area, it adds up to the full weight. Air keeps leaking out under the skirt, so the fan never stops.",
